WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.339
Bias is not a moral failure or proof that someone is careless.

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:05.399
In critical thinking,

00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:09.992
bias means a predictable judgment tendency that can shape how people notice evidence,

00:00:09.992 --> 00:00:12.465
interpret it, and decide what to do.

00:00:12.465 --> 00:00:16.704
Because bias is common, the useful question is not who has bias.

00:00:16.704 --> 00:00:20.591
The useful question is what process helps us reduce avoidable distortion.

00:00:20.591 --> 00:00:25.890
Confirmation bias is the tendency to favor information that supports an existing belief or hypothesis.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.950
In security work,

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.896
an analyst may focus on evidence that confirms an early theory about an incident.

00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:32.602
In leadership,

00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:38.255
a manager may notice examples that support a view about a team while missing contrary evidence.

00:00:38.255 --> 00:00:42.494
The countermeasure is to ask what evidence would change our mind and

00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:44.967
what alternative explanation also fits the facts.

00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:49.207
Anchoring makes an initial number, diagnosis, or opinion exert too much influence.

00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:53.446
Availability makes recent or vivid examples feel more likely than they are.

00:00:53.446 --> 00:00:55.919
Overconfidence makes people stop checking too early.

00:00:55.919 --> 00:01:00.512
Sunk cost makes it hard to abandon a weak path because time, money,

00:01:00.512 --> 00:01:02.632
or reputation has already been invested.

00:01:02.632 --> 00:01:06.871
Motivated reasoning pulls analysis toward the answer people want to be true.

00:01:06.871 --> 00:01:08.284
Groupthink adds social pressure.

00:01:08.284 --> 00:01:13.230
Teams may avoid disagreement because they want harmony, speed, or approval from senior people.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.470
A group can become confident because everyone is repeating the same assumption,

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.590
not because the evidence is strong.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.063
That is why structured review is valuable.

00:01:22.063 --> 00:01:25.595
It gives permission to surface alternatives before commitment becomes expensive.

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:28.068
Bias reduction does not require perfect rationality.

00:01:28.068 --> 00:01:31.248
Practical methods include checklists, independent review, alternative hypotheses, pre-mortems,

00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:33.014
explicit assumptions, and evidence checks.

00:01:33.014 --> 00:01:35.841
The goal is not to remove human judgment.

00:01:35.841 --> 00:01:41.140
The goal is to support judgment with habits that make reasoning more visible and correctable.
